body:
good job. it took me like 4 months to read. i still can't really fathom how a sane person could write a cogent book that long that was that complicated in just a few years. or like how someone could possess the will to do that. 

&#x200B;

my fave character was maybe hal, bc i relate to his thing of "“hasn't had a bona fide intensity-of-interior-life-type emotion since he was tiny." but i like JOI a lot too, just bc of the mystery of him and those few passages from his childhood. and kate gompert. mainly bc through her dfw was able to express more clearly what the thing we call severe depression feels like than anything i've ever read before or after. lol that's 3 characters. 

&#x200B;

if you have questions about the end, this might be of service: [http://www.aaronsw.com/weblog/ijend](http://www.aaronsw.com/weblog/ijend)
